c. protect, provide a sense of security for victims of acts of violence; d. provide services to victims of violence; and
e. implement comprehensive recovery for victims.

Article 10
(1) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 9, shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual matters; and
g. public peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

